    },
    {
      "text": "μ, an improper ﬂat prior is used. We adopt a pragmatic point of view according to which the practitioner,",
      "bbox": [
        48.08934783935547,
        104.4837417602539,
        443.59991455078125,
        113.54876708984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "especially for a small number of parameters, is invariant to maximum likelihood or Bayesian inference but",
      "bbox": [
        48.08934783935547,
        115.19950103759766,
        443.6107177734375,
        123.5113525390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is mostly worried about the comptutational efﬁciency of the methods. Our simulation and prior speciﬁca-",
      "bbox": [
        48.08934783935547,
        125.1620864868164,
        443.6061706542969,
        133.47393798828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tion set-up is such that the posterior mean and precision estimates coincide with the maximum likelihood",
      "bbox": [
        48.08934783935547,
        135.1246795654297,
        443.6061706542969,
        143.4365234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and observed information estimates respectively, and the exact values are available by using the Kalman",
      "bbox": [
        48.08934783935547,
        145.08726501464844,
        443.6026611328125,
        153.39910888671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ﬁlter (KF). The bootstrap ﬁlter is used in all the SMC algorithms.",
      "bbox": [
        48.08934783935547,
        155.0498504638672,
        296.6289367675781,
        163.3616943359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For various values of T, Table 1 shows a comparison of parameter estimates by the particle methods",
      "bbox": [
        57.055747985839844,
        165.01243591308594,
        443.60076904296875,
        173.32427978515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and KF. In this problem the SPF and PG methods show remarkable robustness to the length of the series",
      "bbox": [
        48.08934783935547,
        174.9750213623047,
        443.60076904296875,
        183.286865234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "in terms of the accuracy of the estimates. The mixing time of the latter does not show deterioration with",
      "bbox": [
        48.08934783935547,
        184.9375762939453,
        443.60626220703125,
        193.24942016601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "T (note that the mixing time of the limiting algorithm with T =∞does not arbitrarily deteriorate with T",
      "bbox": [
        48.08934783935547,
        194.14694213867188,
        443.6008605957031,
        203.21197509765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "either; see Papaspiliopoulos et al. (2003) for details). We also varied the signal-to-noise ratio and report",
      "bbox": [
        48.088470458984375,
        204.86268615722656,
        443.60357666015625,
        213.17453002929688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "our ﬁndings in Table 2.",
      "bbox": [
        48.08845520019531,
        214.8252410888672,
        135.45709228515625,
        223.1370849609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
